  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Foro Internacional de Mujeres Ind&#xED;genas (FIMI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Indigenous Women&#x2019;s Forum (IWF) is a global mechanism that brings together indigenous women activists and human rights leaders from around the world &#x2013; Asia, Africa, the Americas, the Arctic and the Pacific &#x2013; to develop a common political agenda, build capacity and develop indigenous women&#x2019;s leadership. The AYNI Fund is the philanthropic arm of IWF and is the only global fund created and managed by and for indigenous women. The movements and organizations supported work for indigenous women&#x2019;s rights on issues such as leadership development, political participation, anti-violence, environmental rights and natural resource protection, land rights/ownership, protection of women human rights defenders, intersections with LBTQI rights and disability rights.</narrative>
  </description>
